      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix login-shell probe cleanup",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Defer login-shell PATH capture until Codex RPC launch, while preserving it for explicit script wrappers such as `#!/usr/bin/env node`.\n- Adopt raw `posix_spawn` PATH probes into `SpawnedProcessGroup`, cleaning helpers that escape the original session on timeout and normal exit.\n- Prevent cross-probe pipe inheritance with atomic close-on-exec pipes on Linux and a serialized Darwin pipe/spawn boundary using `POSIX_SPAWN_CLOEXEC_DEFAULT`.\n- Add regression coverage for native and script overrides, session-escaped output holders, and close-on-exec descriptors.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe PATH runner only killed the original process group. Shell startup helpers could call `setsid()`, retain a probe output pipe, and survive cleanup. Moving PATH capture later avoided unnecessary work for native overrides, but treating every explicit override alike broke script launchers that depend on login-shell PATH. Pipe descriptors also had a small creation-to-`fcntl` inheritance window when probes overlapped.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `make check`\n  - SwiftFormat: 0 files require formatting\n  - SwiftLint: 0 violations in 1,428 files\n- `make test` through autoreview on fixup commit `ffe09726c`\n  - 640/640 selections\n  - 54/54 groups passed on first attempt\n  - 0 failures, retries, or timeouts\n- Post-main-merge exact head `9c21ad784`\n  - focused resolver/process suite: 80 tests in 6 suites passed\n  - `make check`: clean\n- Autoreview: no accepted or actionable findings; correctness confidence 0.91.\n- Original isolated before/after runtime proof and hashed artifacts: https://gist.github.com/anagnorisis2peripeteia/1b3ab2a0f2ee613c442f26e4f72507a7\n\nScreenshots are not applicable because this is subprocess lifecycle behavior.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThe separately observed Codex `auth.json` deletion is unrelated. This patch does not read, write, refresh, or remove Codex authentication state. Validation used isolated homes and test doubles without real account, browser-cookie, or Keychain access.\n\n## Related\n\n- Follow-up to #821\n- Builds on terminal isolation work in #2074\n- Reproduction: https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar/issues/821#issuecomment-4957600350\n\nAuthored with Claude; maintainer fixups by @steipete.\n",
        "branch": "codex/fix-path-probe-timeout-descendants",
